    + \alpha \left( \frac{d\lambda}{dH} \cdot T \right)^2 + V_{\text{geom}}(\lambda) \Biggr]
\end{multline}
where $\lambda$ is the parameter along the filament, $H$ represents the coordinate within the 4D lattice, $T$ is the torsion vector, and $F_{\text{braid}}$ accounts for the interaction between interwoven filaments. The geometric potential $V_{\text{geom}}(\lambda)$ accounts for global curvature and non-linear damping in high-density configurations:
